{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 42, :comments ["<b>They shall see</b> — Because HaShem requites most people according to their deeds in this world, therefore the upright shall rejoice, because being upright they are in gladness and do not worry or fear that a trouble like that which came upon the princes shall come upon them, and they hope for good that shall come to them like the rest of the needy." "And the meaning of <b>all injustice</b> — all men of injustice shall shut their mouths, for they have no answer when they see this."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 107, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:39:06.031398096Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}